  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Defined arbitrary-prime GF(p)[x] as one sealed generated owner of both fmpz_mod_ctx_t and fmpz_mod_poly_t on every native platform. Operands are rooted synchronous borrows, exact moduli are compared before each multi-resource call, and every polynomial or aggregate child result is a fresh self-contained owner. Callers never predict variable result capacities. Executable oracles pin normalization, arithmetic, public ZeroDivisionError, monic gcd/xgcd including (0,0), factor leading-unit extraction, monic factors, canonical roots with exact multiplicities, and formatting through 521-bit primes. Native SJMP v1 bytes contain only modulus and coefficients; a distinct SagePack envelope owns the variable, sparse flag, and canonical-parent restoration. The benchmark now reproduces the existing unsigned-word RangeError through the public PolynomialRing API and records Sage 10.9 baselines.",
    "risks": [
      "The public finite-field parent currently exists for arbitrary primes, but polynomial.py classifies moduli above 2^64 as legacy and reaches nmod_poly, which rejects them. This lane deliberately does not wire or alter that shared public path.",
      "Factorization itself is delegated to future generated fmpz_mod_poly_factor declarations; the executable adapter oracle specifies the missing FLINT unit handling and zero behavior, and recreating production factorization in Python would defeat the architecture and performance objective.",
      "The generated FFI schema must ensure extracted aggregate children clone or take ownership of an equivalent context. A child that borrows an aggregate or parent context would violate the no cross-resource lifetime dependency contract.",
      "Windows must expose the same generated FLINT resource rather than an incomplete operation-dependent fallback. WebAssembly still needs the same declaration lowered to owned linear-memory state."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Independently review the Sage 10.9 observations and the resource lifetime contract before integration.",
      "Add a declaration-schema FmpzModPolynomial resource with construction, copy, coefficient access, arithmetic, divrem, gcd/xgcd, evaluation, formatting, factor/roots, and stable serialization. Keep context plus polynomial as one ownership unit and make all variable-size results callee owned.",
      "Wire polynomial.py only after lifecycle fuzzing proves that closing operands, parent objects, and aggregate result resources cannot invalidate escaped polynomial results.",
      "Add the module to pyrightconfig.json and the focused test to test/node-test-manifest.cjs in the integration lane."
    ]
  }
}
